# TypeScript and Web

- Keep strict TypeScript. Do not add implicit `any`, unchecked casts, ignored errors, or `@ts-ignore` without an approved exception.
- Validate environment configuration and external payloads at trust boundaries.
- Keep secrets and privileged operations server-only; make client-safe boundaries explicit.
- Do not globally disable TLS, framework security, linting, type checks, or hydration warnings.
- Enforce authorization server-side and use stable, redacted errors with correlation IDs.
- Meet WCAG 2.2 AA: semantic HTML, labels, keyboard operation, visible focus, contrast, and reduced motion.
- Implement loading, empty, degraded, error, and recovery states.
- Define safe cache behavior and invalidation for mutable or sensitive content.
- Test critical desktop and mobile flows. A defect fix requires a regression test.
